{"id":"y7-flowcharts-l1","label":"7CT.01 L1: Reading and Correcting Flowcharts","steps":[{"id":"title","label":"Reading and Correcting Flowcharts","content":"<div class=\"lesson-title-slide\"><p class=\"lesson-title-kicker\">Computational Thinking</p><h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Reading and Correcting Flowcharts</h2><p>Year 7, 7CT.01</p></div>"},{"id":"objectives","label":"What You Will Learn Today","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">What You Will Learn Today</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Today you will learn how to read a flowchart from its first instruction to its last instruction. You will then build, test and correct simple flowcharts in FlowScratch.</p><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>Name the Start and End, process, and input or output symbols.</li><li>Follow arrows to read instructions in sequence.</li><li>Describe what a simple flowchart will do.</li><li>Find and correct one faulty instruction.</li></ul>"},{"id":"do-now","label":"What Is a Flowchart?","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">What Is a Flowchart?</h2><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><p class=\"lesson-lead\">An <strong>algorithm</strong> is a set of instructions for completing a task. A <strong>flowchart</strong> shows those instructions using shapes and arrows. Each shape has a meaning, so we can understand the instructions before we run them.</p><div class=\"lesson-flow-grid\"><figure class=\"lesson-flowchart\"><figcaption>Start and End</figcaption><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-terminal\"><span>Start</span></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8595;</div><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-terminal\"><span>End</span></div></figure><figure class=\"lesson-flowchart\"><figcaption>An instruction</figcaption><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-process\"><span>Move 50 steps</span></div></figure><figure class=\"lesson-flowchart\"><figcaption>Information out</figcaption><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-io\"><span>Say &quot;Hello&quot;</span></div></figure></div></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Starter practice</h3><p>Use the three shapes on the left to answer these questions.</p><ol class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>Which words usually appear in the rounded Start and End shapes?</li><li>Which shape would contain the instruction <strong>Move 50 steps</strong>?</li><li>Which shape would contain the output <strong>Say \"Hello\"</strong>?</li><li>What do the arrows tell us?</li></ol><details><summary>Check the answers</summary><ol><li>Start and End.</li><li>A rectangular process shape.</li><li>A sloping input or output shape.</li><li>The order in which the instructions run.</li></ol></details></div></div>"},{"id":"teacher-talk-1","label":"Flowchart Symbols and Arrows","type":"stepper","stepperId":"y7flow-stepper-1","stepperKey":"flowchart_symbols","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Flowchart Symbols and Arrows</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Work through each symbol. Read its meaning, look at the example, then say what that shape tells the reader to do.</p><div id=\"y7flow-stepper-1\" class=\"lesson-stepper\"></div>"},{"id":"worked-example","label":"Read Your First Flowchart","type":"stepper","stepperId":"y7flow-stepper-reading","stepperKey":"flowchart_reading","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Read Your First Flowchart</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Begin at Start and follow one arrow at a time. The stepper will show what each instruction means and what happens when the flowchart reaches End.</p><div id=\"y7flow-stepper-reading\" class=\"lesson-stepper\"></div>"},{"id":"activity-1","label":"Build Your First Flowchart","type":"app-link","buttonId":"y7-flow-l1-activity1-btn","appId":"flowscratch","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Build Your First Flowchart</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Recreate the four-block flowchart below in FlowScratch. Drag the blocks onto the canvas and connect them in the same order as the arrows.</p><figure class=\"lesson-flowchart\"><figcaption>Build these instructions</figcaption><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-terminal\"><span>Start</span></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8595;</div><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-process\"><span>Move 50 steps</span></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8595;</div><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-io\"><span>Say &quot;Hello&quot;</span></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8595;</div><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-terminal\"><span>End</span></div></figure><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Before you run it</h3><ol><li>What will the sprite do first?</li><li>What message will appear?</li><li>Which block tells the flowchart to stop?</li></ol></div><div class=\"lesson-app-link\"><p>Use the green flag to run the completed flowchart. Check each prediction against what the sprite does.</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7-flow-l1-activity1-btn\">Open FlowScratch</button></div>"},{"id":"teacher-talk-2","label":"Finding and Fixing an Error","type":"stepper","stepperId":"y7flow-stepper-2","stepperKey":"flowchart_debugging","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Finding and Fixing an Error</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">The requirement tells us what the flowchart should do. We compare every instruction with that requirement, change the incorrect instruction, then test the flowchart again.</p><div id=\"y7flow-stepper-2\" class=\"lesson-stepper\"></div>"},{"id":"activity-2a","label":"Correct the Wrong Distance","type":"app-link","buttonId":"y7-flow-l1-activity2a-btn","appId":"flowscratch","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Correct the Wrong Distance</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Each flowchart contains one error. Read the requirement first, trace the faulty flowchart from Start to End, then identify the block that must change.</p><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Task A</h3><p><strong>Requirement:</strong> Move 60 steps, then say \"Finished\".</p><figure class=\"lesson-flowchart\"><figcaption>Faulty flowchart</figcaption><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-terminal\"><span>Start</span></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8595;</div><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-process\"><span>Move 20 steps</span></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8595;</div><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-io\"><span>Say &quot;Finished&quot;</span></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8595;</div><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-terminal\"><span>End</span></div></figure></div><div class=\"lesson-app-link\"><p>Run the faulty version, make one correction, then run it again. Keep the corrected flowchart available for Task B.</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7-flow-l1-activity2a-btn\">Open FlowScratch</button></div>"},{"id":"activity-2b","label":"Add the Missing Output","type":"app-link","buttonId":"y7-flow-l1-activity2b-btn","appId":"flowscratch","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Add the Missing Output</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">This flowchart is missing an instruction. Read the requirement first, trace the faulty flowchart from Start to End, then identify what must be added.</p><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Task B</h3><p><strong>Requirement:</strong> Move 40 steps, then say \"Ready\".</p><figure class=\"lesson-flowchart\"><figcaption>Faulty flowchart</figcaption><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-terminal\"><span>Start</span></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8595;</div><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-process\"><span>Move 40 steps</span></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8595;</div><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-terminal\"><span>End</span></div></figure></div><div class=\"lesson-app-link\"><p>Use a separate sprite for this task, keeping your Task A correction available too. Run the faulty version, add the missing instruction, then run it again.</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7-flow-l1-activity2b-btn\">Open FlowScratch</button></div>"},{"id":"change-requirement","label":"Change the Requirement","type":"app-link","buttonId":"y7-flow-l1-change-btn","appId":"flowscratch","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Change the Requirement</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A working flowchart may need to be edited when the required result changes. Start with your first flowchart and read the new requirement carefully.</p><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>New requirement</h3><p>The sprite must move <strong>80 steps</strong> and say <strong>\"Finished\"</strong>.</p><ol><li>Change the Move value from 50 to 80.</li><li>Change the Say message from \"Hello\" to \"Finished\".</li><li>Run the edited flowchart and check both changes.</li></ol></div><div class=\"lesson-app-link\"><p>Open FlowScratch and edit the flowchart you built earlier. Start again if your earlier flowchart is no longer on the canvas.</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7-flow-l1-change-btn\">Open FlowScratch</button></div>"},{"id":"plenary","label":"Plenary: Flowchart Symbols","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y7l1-plenary","validatorKey":"y7l1_plenary","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Flowchart Symbols</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Answer without using the earlier slides.</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><h3>Question 1</h3><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l1-plenary-a\">(a) State the purpose of a Start or End symbol. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l1-plenary-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-a\" aria-label=\"Plenary part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l1-plenary-b\">(b) State the purpose of a process symbol. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l1-plenary-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-b\" aria-label=\"Plenary part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l1-plenary-c\">(c) State the purpose of an arrow. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l1-plenary-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-c\" aria-label=\"Plenary part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7l1-plenary-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 3 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y7l1-plenary-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"},{"id":"plenary-2","label":"Plenary: Read the Flowchart","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y7l1-plenary-2","validatorKey":"y7l1_plenary_2","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Read the Flowchart</h2><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><figure class=\"lesson-flowchart\"><figcaption>Study this flowchart</figcaption><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-terminal\"><span>Start</span></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8595;</div><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-process\"><span>Move 30 steps</span></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8595;</div><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-io\"><span>Say &quot;Complete&quot;</span></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8595;</div><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-terminal\"><span>End</span></div></figure></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><h3>Question 2</h3><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l1-plenary-2-a\">(a) State how many steps the sprite moves. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l1-plenary-2-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-2-a\" aria-label=\"Plenary 2 part a\" inputmode=\"numeric\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l1-plenary-2-b\">(b) State the output produced. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l1-plenary-2-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-2-b\" aria-label=\"Plenary 2 part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l1-plenary-2-c\">(c) Name the type of symbol that contains <strong>Say \"Complete\"</strong>. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l1-plenary-2-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-2-c\" aria-label=\"Plenary 2 part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7l1-plenary-2-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 3 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y7l1-plenary-2-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div></div>"},{"id":"plenary-3","label":"Plenary: Find the Error","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y7l1-plenary-3","validatorKey":"y7l1_plenary_3","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Find the Error</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A flowchart is required to move 70 steps. Its process symbol says <strong>Move 20 steps</strong>.</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><h3>Question 3</h3><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l1-plenary-3-a\">(a) Identify the error. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l1-plenary-3-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-3-a\" aria-label=\"Plenary 3 part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l1-plenary-3-b\">(b) State the correction. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l1-plenary-3-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-3-b\" aria-label=\"Plenary 3 part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7l1-plenary-3-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 2 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y7l1-plenary-3-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"}],"validators":{"y7l1_plenary":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*(it |this )?(shows?|marks?)\\b.{0,30}\\b(begins?|starts?|ends?)\\b.{0,20}$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"It shows where the algorithm begins or ends."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*(it\\s+)?(contains?|holds?|has)\\b.{0,20}\\b(instruction|action|step)\\b.{0,10}$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"It contains an instruction or action."},{"suffix":"c","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*(it\\s+)?(shows?|tells?)\\b.{0,20}\\border\\b.{0,20}$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"It shows the order the instructions run in."}],"y7l1_plenary_2":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*30(\\s*steps?)?\\.?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"30 steps."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*complete\\.?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Complete."},{"suffix":"c","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*an?\\s*(input(\\s*(\\/|or)\\s*output)?|output(\\s*(\\/|or)\\s*input)?|io)\\.?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"An input or output symbol."}],"y7l1_plenary_3":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*(the\\s+move\\s+value\\s+is\\s+)?20(\\s+instead\\s+of\\s+70)?\\.?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"The Move value is 20 instead of 70."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*(change\\s+it\\s+to\\s+)?(move\\s+)?70(\\s*steps?)?\\.?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Change it to Move 70 steps."}]},"pseudocodeValidators":{}}